[Music]  this is just a super quick video about  global event 5 blackout that will be  dropping shortly after the one point 8.1  is released on the 12th of April most of  the information here is based on the  recent pts so there is the possibility  that there has been a few changes  implemented since firstly I don't really  know why it's called blackout naturally  when I first heard about it I assumed it  would be something to do with the ingame  lighting similar to what the Reddit user  could death to could get death so cat if  so CAD posted a little while before the  new patch was announced lights out dark  dangerous so for the remainder of this  video I'm gonna swap out the word  blackout for Pikachu as I feel this is a  better representation the global  modifier Pikachu will be active at all  times during the event regardless of  what PvE content you're playing agents  are equipped with shock ammo that stuns  enemies shooting or running builds your  charge meter the more charge the more  damage you inflict based on the pts this  is quite a lot of fun similar to the  assault global modifier it just makes  you feel really powerful you aren't  doing as much damage as an assault but  and this you don't have to worry about  range I'm expecting some pretty good  speedruns coming out of this event the  activity modifier extreme Pikachu can  only be activated when playing through  the missions and content that are  included in the global event playlist  Pikachu behavior plus you can instantly  kill enemies with over charged melee  attacks but if you miss or you mix out  your charge meter you'll stun yourself  and your allies this basically means  that you'll fill up your charge meter by  running and shooting the same as the  global modifier except if you keep going  after your bar is full you'll get  shocked very similar to the way that  shock ammo directive works in  underground the electro-charged melee  attacks can be pretty fun though the  group modifier total Pikachu includes  both the global and group modifiers but  it gives a bit of assistance and keeping  your charge meter down extreme Pikachu  behavior plus your charge meter will  cool down faster when close to other  group members Pikachu loves cuddles  the missions included in the global  event roster are Times Square power  relay Hudson refugee camp general  assembly Lincoln Tunnel checkpoint and  the incursion is Falcons lost  again based on the pts the classified  gear available during this global event  is d3 if NC Dead Eye strikers and  technicians Authority this is also to be  the first global event to allow us to  buy caches specific to each of the  classified sits above not sure of the GE  credit cost of these yet and the pts  they were all free it's likely that if  you are starting from scratch with  collecting these sets that the superior  cache would be the most cost efficient  but when you're down to just your last  one or two pieces that you need the more  specific caches although more expensive  will give you a greater chance of  acquiring the missing pieces with the  global modifier and blackhat Pikachu  just run whatever build you feel  comfortable with as long as you're  running around and shooting this  modifier will only have you doing more  damage but when it comes to the activity  and group modifiers you may want to run  something with a little more  sustainability like nomads or strikers  getting shocked will leave you  vulnerable for a short period of time  probably the biggest tip I can give you  for this global event with these  modifiers is to run an immunizes support  station while standing in the immunize  er you don't have to worry about  shocking yourself when maxing out your  charge meter plus your teammates will be  happy because every time you get shocked  they do too this makes these modifiers a  lot more bearable having to polish your  weapon and worry about your meter really  slows things down and very quickly takes  the fun out of it overall this global  event is pretty fun to play through  there are a ton of new commendations too  but I'm not going to go over any of them  because I'm expecting a little bit of  change here a lot we're based on things  like the leaderboard of which I'm really  hoping they've learned a lesson here  rewards based on a leaderboard will  always lead to increased hacking or  abuse of game mechanics just quickly  before I go the request I put out in the  last video around getting a crew  together to team up on PC was received a  lot better than I was expecting  tons of emails comments and messages on  Twitter  I haven't replied to everyone yet but  I'm getting through them I wasn't really  expecting so many people to be keen so  in order to everyone Justice of asked  for some help from a mate wanderer to  set up a discord channel for the  community I think he's pretty much done  his part he just has to run me through  it I haven't really used discord too  much  so got to make sure I don't just break  it straight away so if I can get some  time I really hope to be able to give a  link out in the next few days otherwise  thanks for watching and I'll see you in  the next one  Cheers  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]

